  "title": "Learner failure between NEWLEADER and UPTODATE leaks an INITIAL ZooKeeperServer",
  "cause": "The update starts the learner's request processors at NEWLEADER with startupWithoutServing (state INITIAL), but ZooKeeperServer/LearnerZooKeeperServer.shutdown skip a server that is not RUNNING or ERROR, so a learner that fails before UPTODATE never stops those processors or fast-forwards its data tree.",
  "trigger": "A learner fails (e.g. read timeout) after handling NEWLEADER and before startServing, then re-joins.",
  "consequence": "Each failed sync leaks the abandoned server's processor threads (3 failures left 3 extra CommitProcessor threads; none on the old revision); the leaked SyncThread keeps writing the shared log after the peer left the session and the peer's election vote uses a data tree older than its durable log (observed in a real trace).",
  "sites": [
    "zookeeper-server/src/main/java/org/apache/zookeeper/server/quorum/Learner.java:syncWithLeader",
    "zookeeper-server/src/main/java/org/apache/zookeeper/server/ZooKeeperServer.java:shutdown",
    "zookeeper-server/src/main/java/org/apache/zookeeper/server/quorum/LearnerZooKeeperServer.java:shutdown"
  ],
  "actions": [],
  "invariants": [],
  "premises": [
    "startupWithoutServing leaves the server INITIAL until startServing after UPTODATE.",
    "canShutdown() accepts only RUNNING and ERROR."
  ],
